From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add the SoCCP

Describe the SoCCP and its SMP2P edge, following the vendor sun.dtsi:
IPCC client 46, SMEM items 617/616, remote pid 19, watchdog SPI 167 and
the aggre2 NoC to DDR path. qcom,soccp-dstate points at the TCSR
register the SoCCP reports its D-state in (0x1fda000), so also describe
the TCSR block at 0x1fc0000 as a plain syscon; on SM8750 the TCSR clock
controller moved to its own block and nothing else uses it.

The node is enabled in the SoC file on purpose. The bootloader starts
the SoCCP on every SM8750 board, and the driver has to hold its bus path
until the image it loads is in D3 (see the PAS driver change). A board
that ships no soccp.mbn keeps that vote and still wakes from s2idle.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -665,6 +665,73 @@
 		/* TODO: smem mailbox in and out */
 	};
 
+	smp2p-soccp {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p";
+
+		/* IPCC client 46 is the SoCCP */
+		interrupts-extended = <&ipcc 46
+					     IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_SMP2P
+					     IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+
+		mboxes = <&ipcc 46
+				IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_SMP2P>;
+
+		qcom,smem = <617>, <616>;
+		qcom,local-pid = <0>;
+		qcom,remote-pid = <19>;
+
+		soccp_smp2p_out: master-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
+			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		soccp_smp2p_in: slave-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "slave-kernel";
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The bootloader leaves an early SoCCP image running in D0 with no bus
+	 * vote of its own. The driver holds the SoCCP's path to DDR from probe
+	 * until the image it loads has parked itself in D3, as read from the
+	 * TCSR D-state register. Enabled for every board: without the firmware
+	 * the vote is simply kept, which is what lets the SoC wake from s2idle.
+	 */
+	remoteproc_soccp: remoteproc-soccp {
+		compatible = "qcom,sm8750-soccp-pas";
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 167 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				      <&soccp_smp2p_in 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				      <&soccp_smp2p_in 1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				      <&soccp_smp2p_in 2 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				      <&soccp_smp2p_in 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		interrupt-names = "wdog",
+				  "fatal",
+				  "ready",
+				  "handover",
+				  "stop-ack";
+
+		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+		clock-names = "xo";
+
+		power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_CX>,
+				<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MX>;
+		power-domain-names = "cx",
+				     "mx";
+
+		interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_SOCCP_AGGR_NOC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+				 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+
+		memory-region = <&soccp_mem>;
+
+		qcom,smem-states = <&soccp_smp2p_out 0>;
+		qcom,smem-state-names = "stop";
+
+		qcom,soccp-dstate = <&tcsr 0x1a000>;
+	};
+
 	soc: soc@0 {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 
@@ -2190,6 +2257,11 @@
 			#hwlock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		tcsr: syscon@1fc0000 {
+			compatible = "syscon";
+			reg = <0x0 0x01fc0000 0x0 0x30000>;
+		};
+
 		remoteproc_mpss: remoteproc@4080000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm8750-mpss-pas";
 			reg = <0x0 0x04080000 0x0 0x10000>;
